<title>GERMANY: MOTOR RACING-LEADING RESULTS IN WORLD GT CHAMPIONSHIP.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-LEADING RESULTS IN WORLD GT CHAMPIONSHIP.</headline>
<dateline>HOCKENHEIM, Germany 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results in</p>
<p>the opening round of the World GT championship on Sunday:</p>
<p>(race distance 113 laps of 6.834 km circuit)</p>
<p>1. J.J. Lehto (Finland)/Steve Soper (Britain) McLaren-BMW four</p>
<p>hours one minute and 14.596 secs (average speed 201.81 kph)</p>
<p>2. Jean-Marc Gounon/Pierre-Henri Raphanel (France) McLaren-BMW</p>
<p>one minute 33.159 secs behind</p>
<p>3. John Nielsen (Denmark)/Thomas Bscher (Germany) McLaren-BMW</p>
<p>112 laps</p>
<p>4. Hans Stuck (Germany)/Thierry Boutsen (Belgium) Porsche 112</p>
<p>laps</p>
<p>5. Ralf Kelleners (Germany)/Yannick Dalmas (France) Porsche 111</p>
<p>laps</p>
<p>6. Pedro Lamy (Portugal)/Bob Wollek (France) Porsche 110 laps</p>
<p>7. Pierluigi Martini/Christian Pescatori (Italy) Porsche 110</p>
<p>laps</p>
<p>8. Christophe Bouchut(France)/Carl Rosenblad (Spain) Porsche</p>
<p>110 laps</p>
<p>9. Emmanuel Collard (France)/Juergen  van Gartzen (Germany)</p>
<p>Porsche 109 laps</p>
<p>10. Olivier Beretta (Monte Carlo)/Philippe Gache (France)</p>
<p>Chrysler Viper 105 laps</p>
</text>
